iterations.reply:
I left out the metadata fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `LLMClient<inference>`, and that clause is its entire authority. Adding an `http-client` import would exceed that grant even with the platform team's approval, so the approval has to be recorded in the graph's `with` clause and host allowlist first. Also, the URL would embed the raw message text unencoded, so user input could add query parameters. Once the grant is updated, the fetch should percent-encode the text. The output below is the node as specified.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{raw-message, customer-query};

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(message: raw-message) -> customer-query;
}
```

